#
# OCI 11.2's `SELECT CASE WHEN :1 IS NULL THEN 'null' ELSE 'set' END FROM dual`
# binding BFILENAME('PYO_MISSING_DIR', 'pyo_missing_file.txt') as fetched
# (#2466): the bind's descriptor a BFILE (114) of 72 bytes, no charset; then the
# define OCI makes for the select item; then the value, a ub4 of 55 and the
# 55-byte locator, its ub2 length in front, as the row carried it.
# Captured 2026-11-07 through tools/capture_proxy.py: an OCI 11.2 program
# (instant client 11.2, x86-64 Linux, the client charset AL32UTF8; a BFILE
# locator fetched into an OCI_DTYPE_FILE descriptor, then bound SQLT_BFILE by
# OCIBindByPos, called through ctypes) on Oracle 11g XE 11.2.0.2 with
# SERVER=POOLED, the DRCP pool started. The TTC payload, without the packet's
# header, as `hexdump -C` output; the offset column and the |ascii| gutter are
# ignored by tests.replay.parse_hexdump.
